<div class="container">

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Transport Overview</div>
<div class="section-content">
Post-release transportation is coordinated following official release authorization by detention personnel. Transport services are structured to ensure safe relocation, compliance with supervision conditions, and timely arrival at designated destinations.
</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Authorized Transport Types</div>
<div class="section-content">

<div class="box">
<strong>Standard Local Release Transport</strong><br>
Facility to verified residence or intake location within county limits.<br>
<strong>Estimated Cost:</strong> $75 – $150
</div>

<div class="box">
<strong>Regional Transport</strong><br>
Transport to surrounding counties or approved supervision facilities.<br>
<strong>Estimated Cost:</strong> $150 – $350
</div>

<div class="box">
<strong>Long-Distance / State Transfer</strong><br>
Inter-county or out-of-region transport requiring extended supervision routing.<br>
<strong>Estimated Cost:</strong> $350 – $900
</div>

<div class="box">
<strong>Program Intake Transport</strong><br>
Direct transport to assigned pretrial program intake facility.<br>
<strong>Estimated Cost:</strong> $100 – $275
</div>

</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Transport Procedure</div>
<div class="section-content">

<div class="box">
1. Release authorization is confirmed by detention personnel<br>
2. Identity and casefile verification is completed<br>
3. Assigned transport type is determined by pretrial officer<br>
4. Destination and route are logged into supervision system<br>
5. Transport is executed by authorized personnel or approved third-party provider
</div>

</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Compliance & Monitoring</div>
<div class="section-content">

<div class="box">
• All transported individuals remain under pretrial supervision<br>
• Route deviations or unauthorized stops are prohibited<br>
• Electronic monitoring may be initiated prior to or during transport<br>
• Arrival confirmation is required upon destination entry
</div>

</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Legal & Operational Notice</div>
<div class="section-content">

<div class="box">
Transport coordination is conducted under pretrial administrative authority and in accordance with applicable county procedures. All transportation actions are documented and subject to review by supervising personnel.
</div>

<div class="box">
Failure to comply with transport instructions, misrepresentation of destination, or interference with assigned transport procedures may result in immediate enforcement action, including revocation of release eligibility.
</div>

<div class="box">
Transport services may be fulfilled by contracted providers, licensed operators, or authorized representatives acting under direction of pretrial services. Availability, timing, and routing are subject to operational conditions and security considerations.
</div>

</div>
</div>

<div class="section">
<div class="section-header">Important Notice</div>
<div class="section-content">
All transport fees, where applicable, must be processed and cleared in accordance with pretrial financial procedures prior to execution of service. Scheduling is dependent on facility release timelines and personnel availability.
</div>
</div>

</div>

